  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The gate is underspecified: selected blocks, receptive-field sizes, projection sharing, normalization, initialization and regularization are missing. Residual states contain overlapping context, so their weights cannot directly establish which historical interactions matter.",
    "The evaluation plan lacks baseline validation HR@10, a bounded trial budget and controls comparing learned gating with fixed averaging and a parameter-matched baseline. Repeated selection on 200 validation users per category risks validation overfitting.",
    "Mean embedding cosine near zero does not rule out low-rank collapse. Sampled training margins and simulator feedback do not establish that stale context causes validation errors. Originality, potential and difficulty ratings remain provisional."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify architectural precedent and define a reproducible gate that preserves NextItNet causality.",
      "query": "What prior work combines intermediate residual dilated causal convolution states using positionwise softmax gates in sequential recommendation? Compare NextItNet and user-adaptive layer selection, including receptive-field overlap, gate initialization, feature normalization, left-padding masks, and normalization choices that avoid future-position leakage."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Identify controls that distinguish adaptive context selection from additional capacity and limit validation selection bias.",
      "query": "For a single NextItNet model per category evaluated by macro HR@10 on four fixed Amazon validation sets of 200 users and 99 negatives each, what ablations and paired uncertainty estimates distinguish learned receptive-field gating from fixed layer averaging and a parameter-matched baseline? How should repeated validation selection be controlled under a fixed GPU budget without changing seeds or accessing test labels?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Strengthen the evidence linking the proposed mechanism to the observed failures.",
      "query": "Which diagnostics reliably detect representation collapse and excessive dependence on stale history in causal sequential recommendation? Explain limitations of mean pairwise item-embedding cosine and sampled training margins, and assess effective rank, singular-value spectra, gate entropy, and history-truncation sensitivity as supporting diagnostics without treating gate weights as causal explanations."
    }
  ]
}
